{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "d64a384a-1301-8e29-87ef-e148c9199131",
  "created_at": "2026-01-12T12:43:18-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Utilities",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Sean Brennan",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Priya Raman",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:41:30-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Utilities billing, this is Priya. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:41:34-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, hi. Sean Brennan, I'm calling about the water and sewer bill at 348 Spring Street. It came in double. Like, almost exactly double what it always is."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:41:44-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Is the account in your name, Mr. Brennan?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:41:48-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, it's still in my wife's name. She passed, and we never switched it over. So it says her name on it. Anyway, double. I haven't changed anything. Same people, same showers, same everything. I can't figure it out."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:42:01-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'm sorry for your loss. We can look at the account. I'll pull up the last few readings and compare them. One moment."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:42:09-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure. [pause] Ma, ka bu kre? Dja ta bai, dja ta bai, un minutu. Sorry, my mother, she's asking about lunch. I'm on speaker, I'm in the kitchen."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:42:18-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem. I see the current reading is quite a bit higher than the previous quarter. I'll note it for a re-read request so someone can verify the meter. Would you like that?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:42:29-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, do that. Because I'm not paying double for nothing. And while you've got me, can I just pay this at a bank? Like, which places take it? I don't want to mail it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:42:40-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, payments can be made at the collections window here at City Hall, or by mail. I'm not certain which local banks accept them, so I wouldn't rely on that. The bill itself lists where payments are accepted."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:42:53-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, I'll look on the back. [crosstalk] Hold on, what? Yeah, Ma, I'll get them. Sorry. I gotta get keys copied too, at the hardware counter, so I'm going out anyway."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:43:03-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Understood. I've put in the meter re-read request for 348 Spring Street. Is 401-555-0189 the best number?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:43:09-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's it, yep."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:43:11-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good. Someone will call you once the reading is checked. Anything else today?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T12:43:16-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, that's it. Thanks."
    }
  ],
